## Why This Is Asked

Assesses offline-first design, delta-based syncing, and conflict handling under intermittent connectivity, which are critical in collaboration apps used by teams.

## Key Concepts

- Core Data data model for Comment and Patch objects
- Delta/patch format including baseVersion, changes, and timestamps
- Reconciliation strategy (latest-writer-wins or server-validated merges)
- Robust test plan for offline edits, re-connect, and concurrency

## Code Example

```javascript
// Swift-like pseudocode: apply a patch to a Comment
func apply(patch: Patch, to comment: inout Comment) {
    // Validate base version matches current state
    guard patch.baseVersion == comment.version else {
        // Handle conflict resolution
        resolveConflict(patch: patch, comment: &comment)
        return
    }

    // Apply delta changes
    for change in patch.changes {
        switch change.type {
        case .insert:
            comment.text.insert(change.text, at: change.position)
        case .delete:
            comment.text.removeSubrange(change.range)
        case .replace:
            comment.text.replaceSubrange(change.range, with: change.text)
        }
    }

    // Update version and timestamps
    comment.version += 1
    comment.updatedAt = Date()
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design an offline-first image pipeline with robust caching, memory management, and accessibility in a real UI scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Two-tier caching (memory + disk)
- LRU eviction under memory pressure
- Prefetching and cancellation tied to visible cells
- Accessibility: Dynamic Type and VoiceOver labels
- Async/await data loading and main-thread UI updates

## Code Example
```swift
import UIKit

actor ImageLoader {
    private let memCache = NSCache<NSString, UIImage>()
    private let fileManager = FileManager.default
    private let diskDir: URL

    init(diskFolder: URL) { self.diskDir = diskFolder }

    func load(from url: URL) async -> UIImage? {
        let key = url.absoluteString as NSString
        if let image = memCache.object(forKey: key) { return image }
        let path = diskDir.appendingPathComponent(url.lastPathComponent)
        if let data = try? Data(contentsOf: path), let image = UIImage(data: data) {
            memCache.setObject(image, forKey: key)
            return image
        }
        guard let (data, _) = try? await URLSession.shared.data(from: url),
              let image = UIImage(data: data) else { return nil }
        memCache.setObject(image, forKey: key)
        try? data.write(to: path)
        return image
    }
}
```
